OpenCode CLI tool descriptions and JSON schemas

Upstream: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
Source revision: 00e7472faa2ef15b30db6110440117e4e7e1a72a
License: MIT (see LICENSE in this directory)

The embedded ../../opencode_tools.json contains model-facing definitions only,
not executable tool implementations. Definitions originate from OpenCode's
packages/core/src/tool/plugin/ and packages/core/src/codemode/ sources.
The compatibility snapshot was obtained from:
https://github.com/jasonxu114514/opencode2api/blob/d04ff337d73403f446b39289a93343ac6d512260/internal/gateway/opencode_tools.json

The snapshot preserves the official client's descriptions and JSON schemas,
including its Linux/bash shell description, dynamic subagent description, and
2026 web-search description. Preserve these strings when updating the data;
the /inference free-tier gate compares recognized tool definitions with the
official client byte-for-byte, so incomplete or reworded definitions are
rejected.

The embedded JSON remains MIT-licensed and is independent of the transport.
The captured v1/v2 prompts and complete tool sets in internal/opencodecompat
were obtained from opencode2api revision
b8b1454a0ef505d023f2e53e5193671ee7f30c13 (2026-10-25). Those assets contain
OpenCode model-facing text and schemas only; the adaptation code is covered by
internal/opencodecompat/NOTICE.
The Bun-compatible TLS/HTTP transport lives in internal/bunhttp and is ported
from opencode2api under GPL-3.0-or-later; see its NOTICE. Runtime dependencies
added for that transport are permissively licensed:
github.com/refraction-networking/utls (BSD-3-Clause),
github.com/andybalholm/brotli (MIT), github.com/klauspost/compress (Apache-2.0),
and golang.org/x/net (BSD-3-Clause).
